# ACL Specifications

All architectural and operational decisions for this repository are documented
in `docs/specifications.md`. This file is the single source of truth.

## When to consult

- Before creating or renaming playbooks, roles, job templates, or CaC files
- Before changing naming conventions or directory structure
- When answering questions about how the repository is organized
- When proposing new content or consolidation

## When to update

If a decision changes (e.g. new naming convention, different CaC collection,
new exclusion), update `docs/specifications.md` in the same commit as the
code change. Keep the spec and the code in sync.

## Key decisions (quick reference)

- Flat `playbooks/` with `linux-`/`win-` prefix; no subdirectories
- Roles at `roles/` with GPA-prefixed defaults and embedded README
- CaC via `infra.aap_configuration`; credentials/hosts managed outside CaC
- All site-specific values in `controller_config/site_config.yml` (gitignored)
- `Default execution environment` for all job templates
